From: OpenATV STB Kodi Team
Subject: [PATCH] settings: keep STB profiles on media/hdd

The shell wrapper exports KODI_DATA, but kodi-standalone and direct kodi.bin
invocations can bypass that wrapper.  Receiver flash is too small for Kodi's
profile and binary add-on data, so make the STB core default authoritative.

Non-STB Linux builds retain the upstream HOME/KODI_DATA behaviour.

---
 xbmc/settings/SettingsComponent.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/settings/SettingsComponent.cpp b/xbmc/settings/SettingsComponent.cpp
index 30b24c8b21..5f3674d87b 100644
--- a/xbmc/settings/SettingsComponent.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/settings/SettingsComponent.cpp
@@ -88,6 +88,9 @@ bool InitDirectoriesLinux(UserDirectoriesLocation loc)
   const char* envAppTemp = "KODI_TEMP";
 
   std::string userHome;
+#if defined(TARGET_STB)
+  userHome = "/media/hdd/.kodi";
+#else
   if (getenv("KODI_DATA"))
     userHome = getenv("KODI_DATA");
   else if (getenv("HOME"))
@@ -99,6 +102,7 @@ bool InitDirectoriesLinux(UserDirectoriesLocation loc)
     userHome = "/root";
     userHome.append("/" + dotLowerAppName);
   }
+#endif
 
   std::string strTempPath;
   if (getenv(envAppTemp))
